Subject: iOS: GE Plus's startup notices keep the run loop turning, and do not draw in the background

upstream converts the player's GoldenEye ROM (gexPlusRomConvert) and unpacks
the GoldenEye XBLA archive (gebeanUnpackAtStartup) and the Community Edition
patch (gebeanCePrepareAtStartup) at startup, each on a worker thread, while
the game thread draws gexPlusRomNotice() every 16 ms. On a desktop that is
all a window needs. On iOS the game thread is UIKit's main thread, and
nothing in those loops turns its run loop: for the whole conversion (1.7 s on
the lane-3 simulator) or unpack (7 s there, longer on a phone) the app does
not answer the system at all - a resign-active or a background is not
delivered until it ends, and the shell's synchronous pd.ini + eeprom save
on resign cannot run until then. The notice itself draws fine (measured, see
D-071), so the first half of the fix is one SDL_PumpEvents() per notice call
on iOS, which is SDL's own way of turning the UIKit run loop.

The second half (D-075): once a background IS delivered, the shell suspends
the renderer and the display-link pacer, and the game loop's frames stop at
the pacer. These loops never reach the pacer - they call videoStartFrame /
videoEndFrame directly - so without a check they would go on issuing GL and
asking for presents for the rest of the unpack while the app is in the
background, which iOS does not allow an app to do with the GPU. The notice
now pumps FIRST and draws nothing while the shell says the app may not
present (pdIosPresentAllowed, app/ios/PDPacing.m); the caller's loop keeps
polling and sleeping, the worker carries on, and the notice draws again when
the app returns to the foreground. Two counters (drawn / held) are exported
for the shell's console bridge.

Every other platform is unchanged.

diff --git a/port/src/gexplusrom.c b/port/src/gexplusrom.c
index 79673ec32..dc6763d2e 100644
--- a/port/src/gexplusrom.c
+++ b/port/src/gexplusrom.c
@@ -236,12 +236,62 @@ static Gfx *noticeText(Gfx *gdl, const char *text, s32 y)
 	return gdl;
 }
 
+#ifdef PLATFORM_IOS
+// app/ios/PDPacing.m: 0 from the app entering the background until it is about
+// to return to the foreground.
+extern int pdIosPresentAllowed(void);
+// app/gfx/gfx_angle_egl.mm: presents so far, for the two log lines below.
+extern unsigned long long pdAngleSwapCount(void);
+
+// Notice frames drawn, and notice calls that drew nothing because the app was
+// in the background; read by the shell's console bridge.
+s32 g_GexPlusNoticeDrawn;
+s32 g_GexPlusNoticeHeld;
+#endif
+
 void gexPlusRomNotice(const char *title, const char *line, s32 done, s32 total)
 {
 	Gfx *gdl = g_NoticeGfx;
 	const s32 barw = 160;
 	const s32 fill = total > 0 ? barw * done / total : 0;
 
+#ifdef PLATFORM_IOS
+	// The game thread is UIKit's main thread on iOS, and every caller of this
+	// notice waits in a loop on it for seconds (the GoldenEye conversion, the
+	// GoldenEye XBLA unpack, the Community Edition patch). Turning the run loop
+	// once a notice call keeps the app answering the system - a resign-active,
+	// a background - while the worker thread does the work.
+	//
+	// And once the app is in the background, the notice must not draw: the
+	// shell has suspended the renderer and the pacer, and the game loop's own
+	// frames stop at the pacer, which these loops never reach. No frame is
+	// started, no GL issued and nothing presented until the app is coming back;
+	// the caller's loop keeps polling (and sleeping 16 ms) while the worker
+	// carries on.
+	{
+		static s32 held;
+
+		SDL_PumpEvents();
+
+		if (!pdIosPresentAllowed()) {
+			if (held++ == 0) {
+				sysLogPrintf(LOG_NOTE, "gexplus: notice held, app in the background (notice frames drawn %d, presents %llu)",
+					g_GexPlusNoticeDrawn, pdAngleSwapCount());
+			}
+			g_GexPlusNoticeHeld++;
+			return;
+		}
+
+		if (held) {
+			sysLogPrintf(LOG_NOTE, "gexplus: notice drawing again after %d calls held in the background (notice frames drawn %d, presents %llu)",
+				held, g_GexPlusNoticeDrawn, pdAngleSwapCount());
+			held = 0;
+		}
+
+		g_GexPlusNoticeDrawn++;
+	}
+#endif
+
 	gDPSetColorImage(gdl++, G_IM_FMT_RGBA, G_IM_SIZ_16b, 320, g_NoticeColourImage);
 	gDPSetScissor(gdl++, G_SC_NON_INTERLACE, 0, 0, 320, 240);
 	gDPSetCycleType(gdl++, G_CYC_FILL);
